1M Images n/a No 0.250\ncumulative 4.0-point improvement over the ViT-L/16 baseline. Each individual change provides a positive impact, confirming the potential of scaling in video self-supervised learning (SSL).\n2.3Pretraining Dataset\nNext, we describe the sources of videos and images that make up our pretraining dataset, and our approach to curating the dataset.\nScaling Dataset Size. We construct a large-scale video dataset by combining publicly available data sources. Using publicly-available sources in this work enables other researchers to reproduce these results. The overall dataset includes ego-centric videos from the Something-Something v2 dataset (SSv2) introduced inGoyal et al.(2017), exo-centric action videos from the Kinetics 400, 600, and 700 datasets (Kay et al., 2017;Carreira et al.,2018,2019), YouTube tutorial videos from HowTo100M (Miech et al.,2019), and general YouTube videos from YT-Temporal-1B (Zellers et al.,2022), which we refer to as YT1B. We also include images from the ImageNet dataset (Deng et al.,2009) to increase the visual coverage of the pretraining data. To enable joint image and video pretraining, we duplicate an image temporally and treat it as a 16-frame video where all frames are identical. During training, we sample from each data source with a weighting coefficient that we determined empirically via manual tuning. The resulting dataset, which we refer to as VideoMix22M (or VM22M), consists of 22 million samples.Table 1lists these data sources and their weights.\nFigure 4(Left) compares the performance of a ViT-L/16 pretrained on VM22M with a similar model trained on the smaller (2 million) VideoMix2M dataset fromBardes et al.(2024). Training on VM22M leads to a +1 point improvement on average performance on visual understanding tasks, compared to VM2M. Performance improvement is more prominent on appearance-based tasks such as Kinetics-400, COIN, and ImageNet, showing the importance of increasing visual coverage for those tasks.\nData Curation. YT1B is a large video dataset, consisting of 1.4 million video-hours, with no curation and minimal filtering compared to smaller video datasets (like Kinetics and Something-Something v2). Because uncurated and unbalanced data can hinder model performance (Assran et al.,2022;Oquab et al.,2023), we filter YT1B by adapting an existing retrieval-based curation pipeline to handle videos. Specifically, we extract scenes from YT1B videos, compute an embedding vector for each scene, and then use a cluster-based retrieval process (Oquab et al.,2023) to select video scenes according to a target distribution, which is composed of the Kinetics, Something-Something v2, COIN and EpicKitchen training datasets. We describe the details of the dataset construction procedure inAppendix A.2. Similar toOquab et al.(2023), we ensure that none of the videos from the target validation sets are contained in the initial, uncurated data pool.\nInFigure 4(Right), we compare the average performance on visual understanding evaluations between a ViT-L model pretrained on uncurated YT-1B data and a comparable model trained on our Curated-YT-1B dataset. Training with the curated dataset yields a +1.4 point average performance improvement over the uncurated baseline. Notably, the Curated-YT-1B-trained model achieves competitive performance relative to the full VM22M dataset at the ViT-L scale. However, larger-scale models benefit more from VM22M training (seeAppendix A.2), suggesting that combining Curated-YT-1B with other data sources enhances scalability.\n6\n表1 VideoMix22M(VM22M)预训练数据集。为构建我们的观测预训练数据集,我们整合了四种不同的视频来源和一个图像数据集。 训练过程中,我们采用针对各来源的采样概率,并对YT1B应用基于检索的筛选,以减少噪声内容(如卡通或剪贴画风格)。\n来源 样本 Type 总时长 是否应用筛选 权重\nSSv2 (Goyal 等,2017) 168K EgoVideo 168 No 0.056\nKinetics (Carreira 等,2019) 733K ExoVideo 614 No 0.188 Howto100M (Miech 等,2019) 1.1M ExoVideo 134K No 0.318 YT‐Temporal‐1B(Zellers 等,2022) 19M ExoVideo 1.6M Yes 0.188 ImageNet(Deng 等,2009) 1M 图像 n/a No 0.250\nViT‐L/16 基线累计 4.0 个百分点的提升。每一项单独的改动都带来了积极影响,证实了视频自监督学习(SSL) 中扩展的潜力。\n2.3 预训练数据集\n接下来,我们描述 构成我们预训练数据集的视频和图像来源,以及我们的方法 来整理数据 et.\n扩展数据集规模。我们通过组合公开可用的数据源来构建大规模视频数据集。在本工作中使用公开可用的数据源 使其他研究人员能够复现这些结果。整体数据集包括来自 Goyal 等人(2017)提出的 Something‐Something v2 数据集(SSv2)的自我中心视频、来自 Kinetics 400、600 和 700 数据集(Kay 等人,2017;Carreira 等 人,2018,2019)的外中心动作视频、来自 HowTo100M(Miech 等人,2019)的 YouTube 教程视频,以及 来自 YT‐Temporal‐1B(Zellers 等人,2022)的通用 YouTube 视频(我们称之为 YT1B)。我们还纳入了 ImageNet 数据集(Deng 等人,2009)中的图像,以增加预训练数据的视觉覆盖范围。为了实现图像和视频的 联合预训练,我们将一张图像在时间上复制并视为一个 16 帧视频,其中所有帧都相同。在训练期间,我们以通 过手动调优经验确定的加权系数从每个数据源中采样。最终得到的数据集(我们称之为 VideoMix22M,或 VM22M)包含 2200 万个样本。表 1 列出了这些数据源及其权重。\n图4(左)比较了在VM22M上预训练的ViT‐L/16与在Bardes等人(2024)较小(200万)的VideoMix2M数 据集上训练的类似模型的性能。与VM2M相比,在VM22M上训练使视觉理解任务的平均性能提升了 +1个百 分点。性能提升在基于外观的任务(如Kinetics‐400、COIN和ImageNet)上更为显著,表明增加视觉覆盖 对这些任务的重要性。\n数据整理。YT1B是一个大型视频数据集,包含140万视频小时,与较小的视频数据集(如Kinetics和 Something‐Something v2)相比,没有经过整理且过滤极少。由于未整理和不平衡的数据可能会阻碍模型性能 (Assran等人,2022;Oquab等人,2023),我们通过调整现有的基于检索的整理流程来处理视频,从而对 YT1B进行过滤。具体而言,我们从YT1B视频中提取场景,为每个场景计算嵌入向量,然后使用基于聚类的检索 过程(Oquab等人,2023)根据目标分布选择视频场景,该目标分布由Kinetics、Something‐Something v2、 COIN和EpicKitchen训练数据集组成。我们在附录A.2中描述了数据集构建过程的细节。与Oquab等人(2023) 类似,我们确保目标验证集中的任何视频都不包含在初始的未整理数据池中。\n在图4(右)中,我们比较了在未经整理的YT‐1B数据上预训练的ViT‐L模型与在我们的Curated‐YT‐1B数据 集上训练的同类模型在视觉理解评估上的平均性能。使用整理后的数据集进行训练,相比未整理的基线模型 平均性能提升了 +1.4 个百分点。值得注意的是,在ViT‐L规模下,使用Curated‐YT‐1B训练的模型相对于完 整的VM22M数据集取得了有竞争力的性能。然而,更大规模的模型从VM22M训练中获益更多(见附录 A.2),这表明将Curated‐YT‐1B与其他数据源结合可以增强可扩展性。\n6\n\n\n Avg. SSv2 Diving Jester K400 COIN IN1K\n70\n75\n80\n85\n90\n95\n100\nAccuracy\nData Scaling\nVM2M - 2 Million Videos VM22M - 22 Million Videos\nAvg. SSv2 Diving Jester K400 COIN IN1K\n70\n75\n80\n85\n90\n95\n100\nAccuracy\nEffect of Curation\nYT1B - Uncurated YT1B - Curated\nFigure 4 Data Scaling & Curation. We train and compare models on different data-mixes. Models are ViT-L/16 trained for 90K iterations using a cosine learning schedule followingBardes et al.(2024). (Left) We compare the performance of a ViT-L/16 model pre